    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (38 tests, 0 failures) and BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `contactPreference` derived field following the existing pattern for read-only computed owner fields (like `locality`, `displayName`, `initials`):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `contactPreference` property (read-only string) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field and it's documented in the API contract.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` that computes the value: `\"EMAIL\"` when the owner has a non-empty email, otherwise `\"PHONE\"`.\n\nBecause the value is derived on read in the mapper, it works for both the `POST /api/owners` response and `GET /api/owners/{id}`, exactly as the `Cp27Tests` acceptance tests exercise it. Both new tests (`corePhoneWhenNoEmail`, `functionalityEmailWhenPresent`) pass and no existing tests regressed.",
